;; text-cardinality — a claim must have at least one canonical-text value
;; (REQ-KG-003 / REQ-KG-012).
;;
;; Booklogic port of the schema:text minCount constraint in assets/shapes.ttl:
;;   sh:path schema:text ; sh:minCount 1 ; sh:maxCount 1 ; sh:datatype xsd:string.
;;
;; minCount >= 1 lowers to a NEGATION: a claim is a violation when NO claim row
;; with that id carries a non-null canonical-text. Both :not triples share the
;; entity var ?c2 so they collapse to one negated group; ?focus is bound by the
;; positive :where, while ?text is FREE — it appears only in the :not. The
;; compiler lifts a free-var negation group into a named ``<name>_present_<n>``
;; helper rule guarded by !is_null(text), then negates it over ?focus. This is
;; required because a plain inline ``not *claim{id: focus, canonical_text: text}``
;; would bind ?text to a NULL cell and wrongly exclude the absent-value row (see
;; scripts/booklogic_kg._compile_constraint_negations). An empty-string value is
;; non-null, so it conforms — matching SHACL minCount "a value EXISTS".
;;
;; MESSAGE NOTE: pyshacl auto-generates the minCount message ("Less than 1
;; values ..."); EXACT pyshacl-message parity is a P2.3 concern. The human
;; message below is clear and stable for P2.2.
(defconstraint :text-cardinality
  :message "Claim must have a canonical-text value (minCount 1)."
  :path "https://schema.org/text"
  :where [[?c :claim/id ?focus]]
  :not   [[?c2 :claim/id ?focus]
          [?c2 :claim/canonical-text ?text]])
